# Repository-level npm configuration.
#
# Corporate egress is TLS-inspected by Netskope, which re-signs every
# certificate with its own root ("CertServiceCA", Netskope Inc.) through the
# tenant intermediate "ca.nhc-ksa.goskope.com". Windows already trusts that
# root, but Node ships its own CA bundle and does not read the Windows
# certificate store, so npm sees an unverifiable self-signed issuer and every
# install fails with SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN.
#
# The fix tells npm which CA to trust — it does not stop npm from checking.
# `certs/netskope-ca.pem` holds the Netskope root plus the tenant intermediate,
# exported from this machine's own trust store.
#
# Scope: this repository only. Nothing is changed for the user account or the
# machine, and `strict-ssl` stays enabled.
cafile=certs/netskope-ca.pem
